    lsm:documentation "A data type of Percent SHOULD identify a number value that is in the subset of real numbers expressible by decimal numerals and represents a value that is scaled upward by 100 so that 1/100 is represented by 1. It MAY contain a single decimal point as punctuation. The decimal point is ALWAYS the US nationalization character (.) in the designated character encoding (UTF-8 assumed when not stated.) It SHOULD be able to contain at least 18 digits. EXAMPLE: A Tax Rate Percent for a rate of .055 be expressed as \"5.5\"." ;
